---
import Beta from '../layouts/Beta.astro';
import Calculator from '../components/Calculator';
---
<Beta title="My Birth Sky">
  <div class="reading-width">
    <header class="beta-intro"><h1>My Birth Sky</h1><p class="lede">Where was the Moon? Try a fictional birth, or use a date and city. Add a local time to see the rising sign.</p></header>
    <p id="rashi" class="small-note">Gregorian dates 2024–2027 · Indian Standard Time (UTC+05:30) · linear Lahiri approximation. Birth details are used for the local calculation and discarded.</p>
    <div class="beta-band"><Calculator mode="birth-sky" client:load /></div>
    <section class="beta-band" aria-labelledby="birth-glossary">
      <h2 id="birth-glossary">What the wheel shows</h2>
      <dl class="fact-line">
        <div><dt>Rāshi</dt><dd>The Moon’s 30° sidereal zodiac sector.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Nakshatra</dt><dd>The Moon’s position in a separate division of 27 equal sectors.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Lagna</dt><dd>The sidereal zodiac sector on the geometric eastern horizon at the entered city and time.</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p><a href="https://packolkata.imd.gov.in/panchang/en/explanation">IMD calendar definitions</a> · <a href="/panchang/">See the same Moon in today’s calendar</a></p>
    </section>
    <details class="source-card">
      <summary>Fictional example · New Delhi, 1 January 2025 at 08:00 IST</summary>
      <p>The example gives Makara rāshi, Uttara Āṣāḍhā nakshatra and Dhanu lagna. The reference’s Dhanu rising interval runs from 06:06 to 08:10. Leaving the time blank includes the brief Pūrva Āṣāḍhā and late Śravaṇa portions of the local day.</p>
      <p><a href="https://www.drikpanchang.com/panchang/day-panchang.html?date=01%2F01%2F2025&amp;lang=en">Published Moon sign and udaya lagna example</a></p>
    </details>
  </div>
</Beta>
